        "original_id": "778cf93a-d73c-5d93-be4e-498279f579bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Crafter, Martin Degville, Tony James\n- Bands: I Killed the Prom Queen, Confession, Carpathian, Bury Your Dead, Sigue Sigue Sputnik, Generation X\n- Roles: musician, singer-songwriter, entertainment manager, lead vocalist, vocalist, lead singer, co-songwriter, bassist\n- Songs: \"Love Missile F1-11\"\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Degville was born on 27 January 1961 in Walsall.\n- In 1986, Sigue Sigue Sputnik had a worldwide hit single with \"Love Missile F1-11\" and released six other EMI singles.\n- Sigue Sigue Sputnik was formed with ex-Generation X bassist Tony James.\n- Martin Degville is the lead singer and co-songwriter of the UK pop band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Michael Crafter is an Australian musician, singer-songwriter, and entertainment manager.\n- Michael Crafter began his music career as the lead vocalist for I Killed the Prom Queen.\n- Michael Crafter is the vocalist of Confession and a former vocalist of Carpathian and Bury Your Dead.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
